== Trivia ==
* '''Mega Mush''' is based off of the Mega Mushroom from ''New Super Mario Bros.'', which would turn Mario giant, grant invulnerability, and allow him to defeat almost anything he touches.
* Originally in ''Antibirth'', [[Anti:Mega Mush|Mega Mush]] didn't gain charges while active, and was unlocked by defeating {{E|Mother}} (then known as The Witness) as every character on Hard Mode.
* Entering the Big chest in Mega Mush form triggers the credits 0.5 seconds faster than normal (tested by entering the Big Chest going from the same position to the beginning of credits and timed with scripts)
* The Mega Mush form makes Isaac's face look similar to [[enboi:Isaac|Flash Isaac]].
* Mega Mush, along with {{i|1up!}}, {{i|Mini Mush}}, {{i|Magic Mushroom}}, and {{i|Super Bandage}} is one of the few items that make a unique sound upon pickup.

== Bugs ==
{{bug|Activating Mega Mush before entering the Knife Piece 2 area will keep the effect active inside the chase area but Isaac will have his normal sized, followed with a huge shadow and will continuously stomp the ground, breaking everything in his way, even pushing away Mother's Shadow.}}
{{bug|If Isaac walks over a {{e|Teleport Pitfall}} while Mega Mush is active a visual bug will occur where the pitfall is destroyed and can no longer harm Isaac however its sprites still remain in the room. When Isaac reenters the room or exits and continues the run, the teleport pitfall works normally again.}}
{{bug|Using Mega Mush in combination with {{I|Suplex!}} makes you grab enemies and move them around until you leave the room. Doing this on any of the Ultra Harbingers or {{E|The Beast}} will make the enemy disappear and render you unable to move at all.}}
{{bug|Activating Mega Mush through {{i|Void}} will cause Isaac to visually revert to normal after leaving the room while still under the item's effects. If Isaac does not have flight, a stomping sound will play and the screen will shake constantly even if he is not moving.}}
{{bug|When Mega Mush times out and Isaac returns to normal size, he may occasionally appear to have no head. Isaac is unable to fire tears in this form and cannot interact with enemies or objects or pick up items. He also cannot interact with trap doors or Crawl Space entrances, causing softlocks. Going into an animation (e. g. by taking damage, using a [[pill]], etc.), or exiting and continuing the run fixes this issue.}}

